 "turn": {
  "createdAt": "2026-11-08T05:06:57.019751+00:00",
  "status": "complete",
  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen has been playing better recently than his ten-round average suggests, and his approach play is the weak part of his game. Over his newest ten rounds (June 9 to September 26) he averages 76.0, which is 4.3 over par across his last ten full 18-hole rounds. His newest five rounds average 74.8.\n\nThe last two rounds were Home course qualifier rounds on September 25 and 26. He shot 74 (+2) and then 71 (-1). Before those, the Poplar Grove tournament in July went 82, 73, 74. The 82 (+10) on July 8 pulls his averages up. His last recorded round was September 26, so there are no rounds in the six weeks since.\n\nStrokes gained, putts and greens cover 8 of those 10 rounds. The two qualifier rounds have no putting or strokes gained data.\n- **Total:** he is at -6.74 strokes per round against a team average of -4.62. Strokes gained has no college figure, and the Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Approach:** this is the largest loss. He is at -4.16 per round, against a team average of -2.33 and the lowest place on the team.\n- **Putting:** he is at -2.06 per round, which is better than the team average of -3.01. He makes 31.88 putts per round.\n- **Off the tee:** he is at -0.32 per round, against a team average of +0.87.\n- **Around the green:** he is at -0.20 per round, close to the team average of -0.15.\n- **Greens in regulation:** he hits 61.11% over 144 holes. That is above the Division I average of 60%, below the team average of 66.25%, and below the Tour figure of 66%.\n\nApproach work is the clearest place to improve. Putting is not the main issue for him, even though the whole team putts below the Tour baseline.",
